    from jsonb_populate_record(null::public.listening_items, $seed${"slug":"c1-assess-a-dark-sky-lighting-trial","title":"Assess a dark-sky lighting trial","level":"C1","status":"published","sort_order":200,"metadata":{"format":"monologue","script_type":"monologue","speakers":[]},"summary":"A council officer separates different findings from a trial of shielded streetlights.","transcript_text":"A common reading of the dark-sky trial is that the lamps have solved the glare problem. The measurements actually show a narrower result: on the two streets where the new fittings were aimed correctly, less light reached upstairs windows. Complaints on the third street did not fall. An inspection there found the lamps were installed at a different angle, and the complaint records don't distinguish light from the street and light from a nearby loading yard. I would keep the shielding specification, correct the installation, and agree a separate observation period with the yard operator. We should describe the successful streets as evidence that the design can work under the right conditions, rather than an assurance that any installation will have the same effect.","category":"Civic","accent":"general","speed_label":"natural","speed_wpm":144,"duration_seconds":52,"audio_url":null,"focus_skill":"inference","tags":["civic","monologue"],"questions":[{"id":"q1","type":"mcq","prompt":"What is the purpose of the officer's briefing?","options":["To assign blame for a complaint","To close inquiries about every road","To retain a promising design while limiting the claims made for it","To replace light measurements with a complaint count"],"answer_index":2,"explanation":"The officer recommends retaining the design and investigating installation and other light while making only a conditional claim."},{"id":"q2","type":"mcq","prompt":"Which conclusion is justified by the measurements?","options":["The loading yard caused every complaint","Shielded fittings reduced light at windows when 